/target
# Nested target dirs: the fuzz harness is its own workspace and builds into `fuzz/target`.
**/target/
# A throwaway build dir for a root test run: `sudo -E env CARGO_TARGET_DIR="$PWD/target-privileged"
# cargo test ...` sends root-owned artifacts here so they never poison `./target`.
/target-privileged
# `cargo llvm-cov`'s rendered HTML report, if you run one by hand.
/target-coverage
**/*.rs.bk
# Crash core dumps (e.g. a linker OOM writes `core.<pid>` to the cwd): never committed.
core.*
*.log
.claude
# Built guest images and the downloaded inputs they are built from (`cargo xtask build-rootfs`),
# never committed.
/artifacts/
# The local vendor mirror of all sha-pinned upstream inputs (`cargo xtask vendor`): a self-hoster
# produces it to build offline; like /artifacts/ it holds downloaded images, never committed.
/vendor/

# ── Scratch / planning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
scratch/

# cargo-fuzz working data (the `fuzz/` crate is excluded from the workspace; `fuzz/target` is already
# covered by `**/target/` above). Corpora and crash artifacts are generated, not committed.
/fuzz/corpus/
/fuzz/artifacts/
/fuzz/coverage/
dist/

# ── Environment & Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Editors & IDEs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.zed/
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
.DS_Store

# ── SDKs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SDKs under `sdk/` are four ecosystems in one tree, and each vendors differently.
sdk/*/node_modules/
sdk/*/target/
sdk/*/dist/
sdk/*/.venv/
sdk/**/__pycache__/
sdk/*/.pytest_cache/
sdk/*/.mypy_cache/
sdk/*/.ruff_cache/
sdk/**/*.egg-info/
*.egg-info/
*.pyc

# The compiled FFI modules
sdk/**/*.node
sdk/**/*.so
sdk/**/*.pyd
sdk/**/*.dylib

# The plan is kept outside the repository, under scratch/.
/ROADMAP.md
